menu "ESP-Claw IM Platform Channels"

config APP_CLAW_CAP_IM_LOCAL
    bool "Enable local / Web IM capability (cap_im_local)"
    default y
    help
        Register cap_im_local for in-process IM (e.g. Web Agent Chat).
        Provides a local IM channel that routes messages through the
        event router without requiring external IM platforms (WeChat/TG/etc).
        Outbound messages are delivered via a registered callback,
        typically connected to the Web Agent Chat UI.

config APP_CLAW_CAP_IM_FEISHU
    bool "Enable Feishu (Lark) IM channel"
    default n
    help
        Enable the Feishu/Lark bot channel for ESP-Claw.
        Uses WebSocket for inbound messages and REST API for outbound.
        Requires Feishu App ID and App Secret to be configured.

config APP_CLAW_CAP_IM_QQ
    bool "Enable QQ IM channel"
    default n
    help
        Enable the QQ bot channel for ESP-Claw.
        Uses WebSocket for inbound messages and REST API for outbound.
        Requires QQ App ID and App Secret to be configured.

config APP_CLAW_CAP_IM_TG
    bool "Enable Telegram IM channel"
    default n
    help
        Enable the Telegram bot channel for ESP-Claw.
        Uses long polling for inbound messages and Bot API for outbound.
        Requires Telegram Bot Token to be configured.

config APP_CLAW_CAP_IM_WECHAT
    bool "Enable WeChat IM channel"
    default n
    help
        Enable the WeChat iLink Bot channel for ESP-Claw.
        Uses QR scan login and long polling for inbound messages.
        Supports text and image sending (no generic file).
        Requires bot_token obtained via QR login flow.

endmenu
